    "durationMs": 289716,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Everything is in place for the automated test suite.\n\n**Implementation** — NestJS 11 + TypeORM 0.3 + PostgreSQL via `DATABASE_URL` (never hard-coded):\n- `POST /links` — validates url (absolute http/https with host) and optional custom code (4–20 of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`), returns 201 `{code, url, clicks: 0}` with the URL echoed unchanged; generated codes are 8 random chars from that charset. Duplicate custom code → 409.\n- `GET /links/{code}` — 200 with `{code, url, clicks}` or 404.\n- `GET /r/{code}` — 302 with `Location` set to the stored URL, click incremented atomically via `UPDATE clicks = clicks + 1` (exactly once per request); unknown code → 404.\n- `GET /links` — `{items, total}` ordered by id (creation order).\n- A global exception filter maps every failure — including malformed JSON from the body parser — to `{error: \"...\"}` bodies, with bad-request payloads upgraded to 422.\n- `start.sh` builds, applies migrations through the TypeORM CLI (`src/data-source.ts`), then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; README documents startup.\n\n**Verification** — a 41-check curl suite passed: all validation/409/404/422 paths, boundary code lengths (4 and 20 accepted, 3 and 21 rejected), url edge cases (`ftp://`, no host, relative, missing). I also confirmed data and click counts survive a full server restart, migrations are idempotent on re-run, 25 concurrent redirects produced exactly 25 clicks, the server answers on the container's external IP, and start.sh works from a different working directory.\n\nOne environment quirk worth noting: this machine sets `omit=dev`, so `@types/*` packages were installed as regular dependencies — they're in `dependencies` in package.json and present in node_modules, so the harness won't need any installs. The test data was truncated, leaving a clean `links` table with the migration recorded."
  }
